      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is one of those features which could be both good and bad. \nThe good would be that you could recognize your friends easier when they change their name. Though because they only allow name changes every three months, this is not that big an issue.\nIt would also be good if you had a stalker or something, to be able to identify them if they change their name. For example, I had someone blocked, but I cannot tell why I blocked them or if I blocked them inadvertently because they appear to have changed their name.\nOn the flip side of the coin, if you're being stalked, and you changed your name to hide from the stalker, then it would be bad if they could see what names you previously went by. I have one friend who has changed their name for this reason.\nI don't really see how the VRChat devs can reconcile these two issues., so its probably best to err on the side of privacy, and allow users to keep their previous names private. \nThough they could of course provide us the option through the web panel to make our previous names visible to other players if we so choose.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
